# Nauss instances with the upper bounds of the literature (not optimal + 1: they are 4 to 13 above the optimum).
# For gapD-25-90-e4 the upper bound 5647 is the optimum itself: the VRPSolver then ends with "Problem infeasible",
# which correctly means that there is no solution with a cost below 5647. See NAUSS_BENCHMARK.md.
# Tip: after a batch execution, call 'grep statistics: out/nauss-literature-ub.out -h | cut -c13-' to get the results as rows for a LaTeX table.
# julia src/run.jl -b nauss-literature-ub.batch &> out/nauss-literature-ub.out
